Ruud, bad news. Our testing found two issues in the DMS message handling for =
amendments, and the fix needs another regression round. Our DMS release there=
fore slips from the end of October to 10 Nov. I am sorry, we saw it only yest=
erday. The test file for 31 Oct stays as planned, it comes from the pre-relea=
se build. Pia will call you this afternoon to discuss what it means for your =
go-live.

Best regards,
Erik Holm
IT integration lead at Nordline

-----Original Message-----
From: Erik Holm <eholm@nordline.example>
Sent: Friday, 25 September 2026 15:40
To: Ruud Jansen
Subject: Re: Nordline DMS release and test file

Hi Ruud, our plan today: DMS release at the end of October, so in time for 3 =
Nov but without much buffer. We can send you a test file with sample declarat=
ions by 31 Oct. It will contain the same message structure as the production =
release. For the end-to-end test with customs on your side we use the pre-rel=
ease build. I will tell you immediately if the release date changes.

Best regards,
Erik Holm
IT integration lead at Nordline

